The graph shows two depreciation methods for an asset.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}
\definecolor{slcolour}{HTML}{EF6068}
\definecolor{dbcolour}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{gridcolour}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\begin{axis}[name=depreciationaxis,width=9cm,height=7cm,axis lines=left,xmin=0,xmax=6,ymin=0,ymax=12000,xtick={0,1,2,3,4,5,6},ytick={0,2000,4000,6000,8000,10000,12000},scaled ticks=false,grid=major,grid style={gridcolour},tick label style={font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont,/pgf/number format/fixed},label style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black},xlabel={Time (years)},legend style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black,draw=none,at={(0.98,0.98)},anchor=north east},samples=100]
\addplot[slcolour,thick,domain=0:6]{12000-2000*x};
\addlegendentry{Straight-line}
\addplot[dbcolour,thick,dashed,domain=0:6]{12000*exp(x*ln(0.75))};
\addlegendentry{Declining balance}
\end{axis}
\coordinate (valuetitle) at ([xshift=-60pt]depreciationaxis.west);
\path (valuetitle) node[rotate=90,anchor=center,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black] {Value (\$)};
\path[use as bounding box] ([xshift=-8pt]current bounding box.south west) rectangle (current bounding box.north east);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
a. Read the purchase price and the value after $2$ years under each method.
b. Find the annual straight-line depreciation from the graph.
c. Between which two whole years after purchase do the graphs intersect?
